FLEET HOME MARKER — read by Agent-One/hooks/routing_footer_check.py

Presence of this file, in the directory a session was launched from or within six ancestors of it,
puts that session inside the routing-footer hook's scope. The hook reads existence only; content is
for humans. It runs in WARN mode: it never blocks, it logs one verdict per reply.

THIS REPO: `aivis-one/aivis`, the product repo of Agent-Aivis (two-role, sovereign). Sessions here
launch from this repository's own root — verified by `pwd` in the live session at the 2026-08-11
landing, not taken from a document.

WHY IT EXISTS: the hook was path-scoped to the overseer's own tree, so it covered Agent-One and
nothing else while looking fleet-wide — every home launches from its own product repo. A roster of
repo paths inside the script was refused because it would go stale by absence the moment an agent is
born or a repo moves, and nothing would report it. Adoption is opt-in by the home, at its own
landing, so scope rides the landing cycle instead of arriving as a broadcast.

THIS FILE CARRIES NO LOCAL PATHS AND NO ACCOUNT NAME, DELIBERATELY — AND THE ABSENCE IS RECORDED SO
NOBODY "RESTORES" IT. **This repository is PUBLIC.** The first version of this file, committed but
never published, also recorded a harness setting that no repository can commit, together with the
operator's Windows account name and two absolute paths on his machine. Publishing those is
irreversible; rewriting an unpublished commit is not. The setting is real and still required — it
now lives in the agent's PRIVATE home instead, and nothing about it belongs in a public tree.
